{
  "_comment": "Value-free tool-argument descriptions, shared by the Python and TypeScript lanes. For each `args` (a JSON tool-argument value): `input_summary` = redacted_input_summary / redactedInputSummary, `arg_key_summary` = summarize_arg_keys / summarizeArgKeys, `tool_args` = arg_metadata / argMetadata, the authorization context's value-free argument metadata (_arg_metadata / argMetadata). null = the helper returns None / undefined. No value may appear in any output. Checked by watchlight-core/tests/test_arg_redaction_fixture.py, watchlight-claude-agent/tests/test_arg_metadata_fixture.py and watchlight-agent-sdk-ts/tests/redaction.test.ts. Integers and floats are both `number`; `bool` stays `bool`. An argument name longer than 128 UTF-8 bytes is cut at the last whole character within 128 bytes, with no marker. `arg_count` is always the full count; `arg_names_truncated: true` is present only when there are more than 32 arguments. Two names that cap to the same string appear once in `arg_names`, and the first one's type is the one in `arg_types`.",
